# rule.prefer.scoped-tests-locally

run scoped tests locally for fast feedback; let cicd shard the whole suite.

⛔ **`--thorough` is forbidden outright**, local or otherwise — `rule.forbid.thorough-test-runs`. this rule says **how to scope**; that one says the widest run is never yours to make.

## .why
acceptance/integration tests are real-brain, no-mock — cost is LLM latency, not logic. a whole suite runs serially in tens of minutes locally; cicd shards it across runners.

## .two levers cut local cost
1. **`path://` prunes the FILE set; `name://` does not.** jest imports every loaded suite before it filters by test name, so `name://` still loads all ~100 files. `path://` loads only the one file. measured: `name://guard-peer` = 101 files/695s vs `path://review.by.guard-peer` = 1 file/104s (~6.7×). reach for `path://` first; add `name://` only to narrow within it.
2. **`criteria: 'SOME'` stops at first green attempt.** `when.repeatably` short-circuits — one green attempt skips the rest (1 LLM call, not 3). `'EVERY'` runs all 3. use `'SOME'` locally; CI still exercises repeats (`rule.require.repeatable-for-llm-tests`).

## .how
- local: always `--scope 'path://…'`; stack `name://` to narrow. start narrow, widen only as needed.
- ⚠️ **the bare invocation is already scoped** — with no `--scope` at all it adds `--changedSince <trunk tip>`, so it selects the tests your branch's own changes touch. `--scope` narrows *within* that; it is not what creates the bound.
- cicd: the full sharded suite runs on every push — that is the gate. ⛔ never reach for `--thorough` to reproduce it locally.

## .the trap
a loose scope falls through to "all" (e.g. hyphenated `path://peer-measurement` matches 90 files). confirm the `matched: N files` line before you wait.

## .the resnap footgun
`--resnap` (`jest --updateSnapshot`) prunes obsolete snapshots in EVERY loaded suite. paired with `name://` (loads all ~100 files), it deletes snapshots across suites you never touched — a silent coverage regression (real incident: 471 cases pruned from 3 unrelated `driver.route.*` suites). never pair `--resnap` with `name://` — always resnap under `path://`, then `git diff --stat __snapshots__/` to confirm only intended files changed. to restore a pruned snapshot, rewrite it to its index bytes (a resnap will not restore pruned cases).

## .enforcement
- a local run left unscoped where you could have named the file = **nitpick** (the bare run is already `--changedSince`-bound; `--scope 'path://…'` is tighter still)
- push that skips the full sharded cicd suite = **nitpick**
- `--resnap` under `name://` or unscoped = **blocker** (prunes obsolete snapshots across every loaded suite)
- ⛔ `--thorough`, in any invocation = **blocker** — `rule.forbid.thorough-test-runs`
